# Prod, containerized — points at the SAME data directory vigil.sh's
# native backend has always used (runtime/data/prod/argentvigil.db,
# stack.db, stack_images/). This is the real prod dataset, not a copy.
#
# HARD RULE, not mechanically enforced by docker-compose.yml itself:
# vigil.sh's native backend and this compose project must NEVER run at
# the same time — both would write to the exact same SQLite files
# simultaneously, the identical two-writer hazard already confirmed live
# once for the old prod/test split (~10 minutes of a container's
# scheduler writing into prod before it was caught). Before
# `vigil-docker.sh up prod`, always `vigil.sh stop backend` (or `stop`)
# first, and vice versa before `vigil.sh start`. `vigil-docker.sh up`
# checks for a running vigil.sh backend specifically when the target
# environment is "prod" and refuses if one is found — see that script —
# but there is no equivalent check the other direction yet (vigil.sh
# itself does not check for a running av-prod-* container before
# starting). Treat that gap as real until vigil.sh gains the same guard.
#
# UPDATE_MODE=live: prod always self-updates from real upstreams via its
# own collector service, same as it always has via vigil.sh.
# REFRESH_POLICY=protected: nothing should ever "refresh prod from prod" —
# refresh-test-db.sh's SRC_RUNTIME_DIR/DST_RUNTIME_DIR model only makes
# sense pointed AT other environments' snapshot targets, never prod as a
# destination. protected here is just the unambiguous, correct value, not
# a meaningfully exercised guard the way it is for a real snapshot env.
#
# Ports deliberately do NOT reuse vigil.sh's 8000/5173 — 5173 is Vite's
# dev server (unbuilt, live-reloading), not what nginx serves here (a
# built static bundle), so treating them as "the same port" would be
# misleading even once vigil.sh's role is retired. Pick real, permanent
# ports for this once you're ready to cut over for good; these are
# placeholders for first proving the containerized path works at all.
#
# API keys (FRED_API_KEY etc.) are NOT set in this file — they come from
# whatever shell you invoke `vigil-docker.sh up prod` from (real, exported
# env vars), same mechanism vigil.sh's bare-process backend already relies
# on. See environments/README.md's "API keys / secrets" section — this is
# a real, live gap for anything meant to run unattended (cron/CI/a fresh
# shell with no keys exported silently boots with empty keys, no error).
AV_ENV_NAME=prod
API_PORT=9001
WEB_PORT=9000
HOST_RUNTIME_DIR=./runtime/data/prod
REFRESH_POLICY=protected
UPDATE_MODE=live
AI_BACKEND=forge
